b. medico-legal services constitute a form of medical service for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
c. psychosocial services constitute services provided by companions in order to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of space and victim houses to protect victims from threats and intimidation for victims;
d. legal services to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process;
e. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.
2. The service mechanism as referred to in paragraph (1) is organized based on Standard Operating Procedures.
